From 38fb92b99e86ad2e98ba7adeb51ed994e6fd6ed9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Fox <timfox@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:19:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] gamecube: retail Half-Life HUD on every route

The client HUD had a quality-0 "lean" mode: CHud::Init only hooked
messages (no HUD elements, no cvars), VidInit loaded no hud.txt, and
Redraw drew a stand-in (health/armor at the top, a permanent pain sprite
and train dial, a fixed green crosshair, 320 sheets). The engine set
gc_quality 0 while the client came up on the New Game routes, so this
was the HUD players got; and once the HEV suit was on and quality was
back at 1, Redraw ran the full path on that half-built CHud and the game
froze (c2a1, 3 of 3 runs).

CHud::Init and VidInit now always do the retail work (every HUD element,
MOTD, scoreboard, menu, hud_draw and the other cvars), Redraw is the
retail one, and UpdateClientData no longer skips the gc_quality-0 probe
path. Only Steam rich presence is left out (retail has none).

The menu New Game route also skipped CBasePlayer::UpdateClientData
entirely, so Health, Battery, WeaponList, CurWeapon, AmmoX, HideWeapon,
SetFOV, Damage and Train were never sent: no health, armor or ammo and
an empty weapon menu. It runs again, as in retail.

Dolphin, retail menu New Game route (c2a1 start, HEV suit and weapons
given through the probe console script; c1a4, c2a4a and c0a0 -> c1a0
campaign rides): no freeze on suit pickup; health/armor/ammo, weapon
buckets, pickup history, flashlight, crosshair and the death HUD match
retail at 640x480.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
